Disk Access Time

When OS reads data:

Total Time =

Seek Time
+
Rotational Latency
+
Transfer Time
1. Seek Time

Time taken to move head.

Example:

Track 10
      ↓
Track 200

Movement time.

2. Rotational Latency

Wait for sector to rotate.

Example

Desired sector not under head

Need to wait.

3. Transfer Time

Actual reading time.

Disk Scheduling

Many requests arrive.

Example:

98
183
37
122
14
124
65
67

Question:

Which request should be served first?
1️⃣ FCFS

First Come First Serve.

Example

98
183
37
122

Serve in same order.

Advantage

Simple.

Disadvantage

Poor performance.

2️⃣ SSTF

Shortest Seek Time First.

Idea:

Choose nearest request.

Example

Current Head:

50

Requests:

10
55
90

Nearest:

55

Choose first.

Advantage

Less head movement.

Disadvantage

Starvation possible.

3️⃣ SCAN (Elevator Algorithm)

Most famous.

Idea:

Head moves in one direction.

Serves all requests.

Then reverses.

Visualization

0 ---------------- 200
      →

Then:

←

Like elevator.

Advantage

Fair.

4️⃣ C-SCAN

Circular SCAN.

Instead of reversing:

0 → 200

Jump back:

200 → 0

Then continue.

Provides more uniform waiting time.

5️⃣ LOOK

Like SCAN.

But doesn't go till disk end.

Example

Last request:

170

Stop at:

170

Not:

200

Less movement.

6️⃣ C-LOOK

LOOK + Circular behavior.

Most efficient practical variation.

Comparison Table
Algorithm	Idea
FCFS	Arrival Order
SSTF	Nearest Request
SCAN	Elevator
C-SCAN	Circular Elevator
LOOK	Smart SCAN
C-LOOK	Smart Circular SCAN
